## Architecture Review
**Verdict:** APPROVED

### AC Assessment
| AC Line | Assessment | Action |
|---------|------------|--------|
| AC1: CancelSlot in cancellation.py with set_source/is_set | Precise: class location, protocol conformance, late-binding semantics, unlinked default all specified | Refined: added method signatures and return semantics |
| AC2: 3 toolsets accept cancel and forward to pipelines | Precise: named classes, methods, and passthrough targets; all pipeline methods already accept cancel= | Keep |
| AC3: bootstrap creates CancelSlot, injects, stores on BootstrapResult | Refined: named specific _build_*_toolset helpers and build_toolsets; BootstrapResult.cancel_slot field | Refined |
| AC4: run_daemon calls slot.set_source(LinkedCancelSignal(shutdown_event)) | Refined: added cancel_slot param on run_daemon signature | Refined |
| AC5: Non-daemon callers unchanged | Clear behavioral constraint, testable by asserting is_set returns False | Keep |
| AC6: All #1002 RED tests pass | Replaced vague "focused tests" with explicit reference to companion RED test task | Refined |

### Architecture Notes
- CancelSlot maps to .NET CancellationTokenSource/Token pattern (.90 confidence per research validation).
- cancellation.py already owns CancelSignal + LinkedCancelSignal; adding CancelSlot keeps the concern co-located.
- Toolset constructors follow optional-param pattern; adding cancel: CancelSignal | None = None is backward-compatible.
- BootstrapResult is a non-frozen dataclass (bootstrap/_types.py:93); adding cancel_slot: CancelSlot | None = None is safe.
- _build_*_toolset helpers in bootstrap/knowledge.py construct toolsets; each needs one extra kwarg.
- run_daemon creates shutdown_event at daemon.py:1073; set_source call goes after that line.
- Existing pattern precedent: RetrospectiveHook already receives LinkedCancelSignal from bootstrap (bootstrap/__init__.py:129-138).
- No security surface introduced: CancelSlot is internal-only, read-only access, single-threaded event loop.

### Failure Mode Map
| CODEPATH | FAILURE MODE | EXCEPTION | HANDLED? | USER IMPACT |
|----------|--------------|-----------|----------|-------------|
| CancelSlot.is_set() unlinked | No source set | N/A | Yes: returns False | Tool ops run without cancellation (same as today) |
| CancelSlot.set_source() | Called after toolset already used | N/A | Yes: next is_set() reflects new source | None: transparent late binding |
| _ingest_document with cancel set | Pipeline exits early | N/A (cooperative) | Yes: partial result returned | Ingest stops cleanly on shutdown |

